  "prefLabel": "Rev 901.09 Dividend",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 901.09 “Dividend” means an amount of property distributed, with respect to their ownership interest, other than in liquidation of the organization, to shareholders or interest-holders of an organization from:\n\n(a) Current year profit; or\n\n(b) Accumulated profits of such entity.\n\nSource. #4557, eff 12-28-88; ss by #5947, eff 12-29-94; ss by #6321, eff 8-22-96; ss by #8137, eff 8-10-04; ss by #9658, eff 2-24-10; ss by #9843, eff 12-23-10 (formerly Rev 901.08) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Rev 900); ss by #10211, eff 10-24-12 (from Rev 901.07); renumbered by #10795 (from Rev 901.08); ss by #13433, eff 8-12-22",
